{
  "title": "Galeazzi Fracture - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4016/galeazzi-fracture--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 12 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Galeazzi Fractures are rare injuries in the pediatric population and consist of distal radius fractures at the distal metaphyseal-diaphyseal junction with concomitant disruption of the distal radioulnar joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with plain radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally closed reduction and casting for the majority of fractures. Surgical management is indicated for irreducible DRUJ due to interposed tendon or periosteum.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "relatively rare injury (3% of distal radius fractures associated with DRUJ disruption)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "less frequent than in adults",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "often missed injury pattern (up to 41%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**when radial fracture is < 7.5 cm from the articular surface, 55% chance of DRUJ instability (6% chance if > 7.5 cm)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "peak incidence 9 to 13 years old",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**DRUJ disruption**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "disruption of the DRUJ in a pediatric patient can consist of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**DRUJ dislocation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "a displaced ulnar physeal injury (Galeazzi-equivalent)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "most common",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4016/images/screen_shot_2018-09-16_at_4.40.28_pm.jpg",
                              "caption": "Galeazzi-equivalent injury with ulnar physeal injury"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "axial loading in combination with extremes of forearm rotation (pronation or supination)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pronation produces an apex dorsal radial fracture with the distal ulna displaced dorsally",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "supination produces an apex volar radial fracture with the distal ulna displaced volarly",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Associated injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "nerve injuries are rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DRUJ",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "osteology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "possesses poor bony conformity in order to allow some translation with rotatory movements",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ligamentous",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ligament structures are critical in stabilizing the radius as it rotates about the ulna during pronation and supination",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "triangular fibrocartilage complex (TFCC) is a critical component to DRUJ stability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "biomechanics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the joint is most stable at the extremes of rotation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Walsh classification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Dorsal displacement of the radius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Due to supination force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Volar displacement of the radius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Due to pronation force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wrist and forearm pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "radial deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "limitation of wrist motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar head prominence or deformity can sometimes be seen",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with movement or palpation of the wrist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "DRUJ instability may be appreciated by local tenderness and instability to testing of the DRUJ",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "compare to contralateral side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "careful examination for nerve injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "required views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and true lateral radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "true lateral radiograph is essential in determining the direction of displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "a slightly oblique view may cause the ulna to appear subluxed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "in a normal wrist, the ulnar styloid should point to the triquetrum in all views, including oblique projections",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "additional views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "contralateral radiographs often helpful for comparison",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "displaced distal radial shaft fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "DRUJ disruption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may be subtle and radiographs must be scrutinized",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**additional signs of DRUJ instability include**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**ulnar styloid fracture**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**widened DRUJ on posteroanterior view**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**greater than or equal to 5mm radial shortening**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction with long arm casting",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**first-line of treatment in children**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "92% of adults experience poor outcomes with non-operative management",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "requires anatomic reduction of both the radius fracture and the DRUJ",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "supination is required for reduction if there is dorsal subluxation of the ulna",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pronation is required for reduction if there is volar subluxation of the ulna",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "immobilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "place in above elbow cast in supination",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "good to excellent with proper reduction of the radius and concomitant DRUJ reduction, even in cases where the DRUJ injury was not initially recognized",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction internal fixation +/- DRUJ pinning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "unable to obtain anatomic closed reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "irreducible DRUJ due to interposed tendon or periosteum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radial fixation can be done with volar plate or flexible IMN (see below)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF, soft tissue reconstruction of DRUJ and TFCC, +/- corrective osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "chronic DRUJ instability (a rare consequence of a missed injury)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "corrective osteotomy with **soft tissue reconstruction of DRUJ and TFCC**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "DRUJ subluxation is caused by a radial malunion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "a corrective osteotomy is also required in addition to reconstruction, otherwise a soft tissue reconstruction of the DRUJ alone will fail",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**ORIF with volar plating, +/- DRUJ pinning**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4016/images/screen_shot_2018-09-16_at_3.55.20_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "Galeazzi fracture treated with ORIF of the radius and pinning of the radius and ulna."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dorsal approach to DRUJ to remove interposed material (ECU) if unable to obtain closed reduction**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "volar approach for ORIF(with plate)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "open reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "irreducible DRUJ requires an open reduction to remove interposed material",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduction can be blocked by interposed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "tendon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**ECU most common interposed tendon**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "periosteum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "DRUJ stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "following fixation, test DRUJ (shuck test)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**if unstable, pin ulna to radius in supination**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**if unstable with large ulnar styloid fragment, fix ulnar styloid and splint in supination**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**ORIF with flexible intramedullary nailing, +/- DRUJ pinning**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "percutaneous (with IMN) of radius fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "open reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "same as above",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "DRUJ stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "same as above",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Delayed diagnosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Malunion/nonunion of the radius**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "commonly a result of persistent ulnar subluxation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Chronic DRUJ instability**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "chronic DRUJ instability (a rare consequence of a missed injury)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "less common in children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
